{"id":"ipsec_checknss.8","n":"ipsec_checknss","s":"8","src":{"r":{"pkg":"libreswan","ver":"4.15-8.el9","repo":"AppStream","url":"https://dl.rockylinux.org/vault/rocky/9.6/AppStream/x86_64/os/Packages/l/libreswan-4.15-8.el9.x86_64.rpm","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/ipsec_checknss.8.gz","sha256":"f51b9805cdc0e94e9ebac6849207810226c40fa7c28dffa30a759675fe412766","date":"01/14/2025","origin":"libreswan"}},"nopt":{"r":0},"desc":"Initialise the IPsec NSS database","r":[["NAME","<p>ipsec_checknss - Initialise the IPsec NSS database</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>ipsec checknss</b> [--nssdir <i>/var/lib/ipsec/nss</i>] [--settrusts]</p>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p><i>Checknss</i> Checks or initialises the NSS database where all private keys for RSA and certificate keypairs are stored. To remove an existing IPsec NSS database, remove all the *.db files and pkcs11.txt from the NSS data directory (default: /var/lib/ipsec/nss).</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>ipsec.conf</b>(5), <b>ipsec</b>(8), <b>ipsec_auto</b>(8), <b>ipsec_initnss</b>(8)</p>"],["BUGS","<p>none</p>"],["AUTHOR","<p><b>Tuomo Soini</b></p>"]]}